description: Read-only quality gates — Pint style check + PHPStan level 6, grouped report
---

Run this repo's two read-only quality gates and report findings. **Modify nothing.** No auto-fixing, no `--generate-baseline`, never run `pint` without `--test`.

1. **Style** — `vendor/bin/pint --test --format agent`
2. **Types** — `composer phpstan`

Scope: `$ARGUMENTS`

- Empty → run both over the whole project.
- Paths given (e.g. `app/Models app/Support`) → pass them to Pint only (`vendor/bin/pint --test --format agent app/Models app/Support`); PHPStan always runs whole-project because its baseline is line-keyed.

Report:

- One finding per line: `path:line` — the rule or message, then the fix in a single clause.
- Group by file, most severe first.
- Clean gate → print exactly `Pint: clean` and/or `PHPStan: clean`. Do not invent findings to fill the report.
- A PHPStan error already covered by `phpstan-baseline.neon` is not new — label it `baseline-covered` and keep it out of the headline count.
- A PHPStan failure whose only errors are `ignore.unmatched` ("Ignored error pattern … was not matched") is a **stale baseline entry**, not broken code. Label each one `baseline-stale: <file>`, do not regenerate the baseline, and do not count it as a code defect.
- Finish with a one-line verdict: `ship`, `fix first`, or `blockers`. Then stop; fixes are a separate request.
